Provenance of the recognition strategy
--------------------------------------

The page-level strategy in `skills/scan2md/scripts/scan2md.py` — bleed-through
filtering by dark-pixel ratio, visual-line clustering, document-wide header and
footer removal, and dot-gated heading promotion — is **adapted from a working
pipeline written earlier in the same user's other workspace**
(`G:\Deepseek生成读书skill区\tools\ocr_book.py`), which had already been validated
against two real scanned Chinese textbooks.

That earlier script established the measured thresholds reused here:

  * ghost text from the reverse side sits at ~0.0% dark pixels inside its box,
    the faintest genuine line (a bare equation number) at ~3.7%;
  * a bare integer at the start of a line is usually a misread Greek symbol in a
    nomenclature list, not a heading, so heading promotion requires a dot;
  * running heads repeat on ≥20% of pages within the top 12% / bottom 15% bands.

This package's contribution is the surrounding engineering: a `probe` command
that refuses documents which already have a text layer, per-page checkpointing
so a multi-hour run resumes, a machine-readable progress log, and a quality
report that names the low-confidence lines.

Runtime dependencies (not bundled)
----------------------------------

  PyMuPDF — Artifex Software, AGPL-3.0
      Page rasterisation and text-layer probing. Called, not shipped or modified.

  RapidOCR (rapidocr_onnxruntime) — Apache-2.0
      PP-OCR detection and recognition. Models are downloaded on first use and
      cached in the user profile, not in this package.

  NumPy — BSD-3-Clause
      Array operations for the bleed-through filter.

  Node.js built-ins only on the JavaScript side — this package has no npm
  dependencies.

